  "id": "COMPOUND:30551 - PROTEIN:1725",
  "verbalization": "Chaetomugilin I is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein through multiple intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Chaetomugilin I directly targets Peripheral myelin protein 22, which in turn is a target of both Longistyline C and 2-(2-((2E)-3,7-Dimethyl-2,6-octadien-1-yl)-5-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-6-benzofuranol. These compounds are likely involved in the regulation of the Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein indicates a potential role in cellular processes involving hemoglobin stability, possibly through the modulation of myelin-related proteins. The integration of these findings highlights the complex network of interactions that may underlie the biological effects of Chaetomugilin I.",
